  <h3>Component Hierarchy</h3>
  <pre><code>App
├── AuthContext.Provider
│   └── AppContext.Provider
│       ├── Router
│       │   ├── /login → Login
│       │   ├── /register → Register
│       │   └── /* (protected) → Layout
│       │       ├── Sidebar
│       │       ├── Topbar
│       │       └── Outlet (page content)
│       │           ├── Dashboard
│       │           ├── ObjectList → ObjectCard[]
│       │           ├── ObjectDetail → FieldList
│       │           ├── RecordListPage → Table
│       │           └── RecordDetail → RelatedList[]</code></pre>

  <h3>State Management</h3>
  <p>Uses React Context API for global state:</p>

  <h4>AuthContext</h4>
  <pre><code>{`${jsonOpen}
  user: ${ jsonOpen} id, name, email, role ${jsonClose},
  tenant: ${jsonOpen} id, name ${jsonClose},
  isAuthenticated: boolean,
  login: (email, password) => Promise,
  logout: () => Promise,
  register: (data) => Promise
${jsonClose}`}</code></pre>

  <h4>AppContext</h4>
  <pre><code>{`${jsonOpen}
  objects: ObjectMeta[],
  currentObject: ObjectMeta | null,
  refreshObjects: () => Promise,
  setCurrentObject: (object) => void
${jsonClose}`}</code></pre>

  <h2>Database Schema Design</h2>

  <h3>Multi-Tenancy Pattern</h3>
  <p>
    Every collection includes a <code>tenantId</code> field. All queries filter by
    tenant to ensure data isolation.
  </p>

  <pre><code>{`// Example query with tenant filter
const records = await DynamicRecord.find(${jsonOpen}
  tenantId: req.tenant._id,
  objectApiName: 'customer'
${jsonClose});`}</code></pre>

  <h3>Dynamic Schema Pattern</h3>
  <p>
    Instead of creating MongoDB collections for each custom object, we use a flexible
    schema:
  </p>

  <pre><code>{`// ObjectMeta defines the structure
${jsonOpen}
  tenantId: ObjectId,
  label: "Customer",
  apiName: "customer",
  fields: [ref to FieldMeta]
${jsonClose}

// DynamicRecord stores actual data
${jsonOpen}
  tenantId: ObjectId,
  objectApiName: "customer",
  data: ${jsonOpen}
    name: "Acme Corp",
    email: "contact@acme.com",
    revenue: 1000000
  ${jsonClose}
${jsonClose}`}</code></pre>

  <h2>API Design</h2>

  <h3>RESTful Conventions</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>GET:</strong> Retrieve resources</li>
    <li><strong>POST:</strong> Create new resources</li>
    <li><strong>PUT/PATCH:</strong> Update existing resources</li>
    <li><strong>DELETE:</strong> Remove resources</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Response Format</h3>
  <pre><code>{`// Success response
${jsonOpen}
  "success": true,
  "data": ${jsonOpen} ... ${jsonClose},
  "message": "Operation completed"
${jsonClose}

// Error response
${jsonOpen}
  "success": false,
  "error": "Error message",
  "code": "ERROR_CODE"
${jsonClose}`}</code></pre>

  <h3>Error Handling</h3>
  <pre><code>{`// Centralized error handler
app.use((err, req, res, next) => ${jsonOpen}
  console.error(err.stack);
  res.status(err.status || 500).json(${jsonOpen}
    success: false,
    error: err.message || 'Internal server error',
    code: err.code
  ${jsonClose});
${jsonClose});`}</code></pre>

  <h2>Security Architecture</h2>

  <h3>Authentication Flow</h3>
  <ol>
    <li>User submits login credentials</li>
    <li>Backend validates credentials with bcrypt</li>
    <li>If valid, creates session in MongoDB</li>
    <li>Returns session cookie to client</li>
    <li>Client includes cookie in subsequent requests</li>
    <li>Session middleware validates and loads session data</li>
  </ol>

  <h3>Authorization Layers</h3>
  <ol>
    <li><strong>Authentication:</strong> Is user logged in?</li>
    <li><strong>Tenant Isolation:</strong> Does user belong to this tenant?</li>
    <li><strong>Role Permissions:</strong> Does role allow this action?</li>
    <li><strong>Object Permissions:</strong> Can user access this object?</li>
    <li><strong>Record Ownership:</strong> Does user own this record?</li>
  </ol>

  <h3>Security Best Practices</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Passwords hashed with bcrypt (10 rounds)</li>
    <li>Session cookies are httpOnly and secure in production</li>
    <li>All queries include tenant filter</li>
    <li>Input validation on all endpoints</li>
    <li>SQL injection prevented by Mongoose</li>
    <li>XSS protection via React's escaping</li>
    <li>CORS configured for frontend domain only</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Performance Considerations</h2>

  <h3>Database Indexes</h3>
  <pre><code>{`// Key indexes
User: ${jsonOpen} tenantId: 1, email: 1 ${jsonClose} (unique)
ObjectMeta: ${jsonOpen} tenantId: 1, apiName: 1 ${jsonClose} (unique)
DynamicRecord: ${jsonOpen} tenantId: 1, objectApiName: 1 ${jsonClose}
Session: ${jsonOpen} sessionId: 1 ${jsonClose} (unique), ${jsonOpen} expiresAt: 1 ${jsonClose} (TTL)`}</code></pre>

  <h3>Caching Strategy</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>ObjectMeta cached in memory (updated on change)</li>
    <li>Session data cached by connect-mongo</li>
    <li>Frontend caches API responses with React Query (future enhancement)</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Query Optimization</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Use select() to fetch only needed fields</li>
    <li>Paginate large result sets</li>
    <li>Limit related list queries</li>
    <li>Use aggregate pipelines for complex queries</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Scalability</h2>

  <h3>Horizontal Scaling</h3>
  <p>Backend is stateless (sessions in MongoDB), allowing multiple instances:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Deploy multiple Express servers behind load balancer</li>
    <li>MongoDB handles session synchronization</li>
    <li>No sticky sessions required</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Database Scaling</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>MongoDB replica sets for high availability</li>
    <li>Sharding by tenantId for large deployments</li>
    <li>Read replicas for analytics queries</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Deployment Architecture</h2>

  <pre><code>Production Setup:

┌─────────────────┐
│   Load Balancer │
│     (Nginx)     │
└────────┬────────┘
         │
    ┌────┴────┐
    │         │
┌───▼───┐ ┌──▼────┐
│App 1  │ │App 2  │  ← Express instances
└───┬───┘ └──┬────┘
    │        │
    └────┬───┘
         │
    ┌────▼────────┐
    │   MongoDB   │
    │ Replica Set │
    └─────────────┘</code></pre>

  <h2>Future Enhancements</h2>

  <ul>
    <li>Redis for session store (faster than MongoDB)</li>
    <li>Message queue for async tasks (Bull/RabbitMQ)</li>
    <li>ElasticSearch for advanced search</li>
    <li>WebSocket support for real-time updates</li>
    <li>CDN for frontend static assets</li>
    <li>Docker containers for deployment</li>
    <li>Kubernetes for orchestration</li>
  </ul>
</DevLayout>
